@md = http://localhost:4004/masterdata
@cargo = http://localhost:4004/cargo

### 1) Should FAIL: IMO typo (9312342, should end in 1)
POST {{md}}/Vessels
Content-Type: application/json

{ "imoNumber": "9312342", "name": "TYPO TEST", "type_code": "CONT", "lengthOverall": 200, "maxDraft": 10 }

### 2) Should SUCCEED: valid IMO
POST {{md}}/Vessels
Content-Type: application/json

{ "imoNumber": "9074729", "name": "COROMANDEL TRADER", "type_code": "GENC", "lengthOverall": 160, "maxDraft": 9.2 }

### 3) Should FAIL: container typo (should end in 3)
POST {{cargo}}/Containers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bl_ID": "11000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "containerNumber": "OCLU1234567", "type_code": "20GP", "grossWeightKg": 10000 }

### 4) Should FAIL: deep insert with one good and one bad container – nothing is saved
POST {{cargo}}/Manifests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "manifestNumber": "EGM-2026-1103",
  "call_ID": "d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "direction_code": "EXP",
  "billsOfLading": [
    {
      "blNumber": "OCLINCOK2611006",
      "cargoType_code": "CONT",
      "description": "Coir products",
      "grossWeightKg": 20000,
      "containers": [
        { "containerNumber": "BWSU3004006", "type_code": "40GP", "grossWeightKg": 10000 },
        { "containerNumber": "BWSU3004012", "type_code": "40GP", "grossWeightKg": 10000 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 5) Should FAIL: PATCH an existing container to a wrong number
PATCH {{cargo}}/Containers(21000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "containerNumber": "OCLU1234560" }